{#
  « Stockage » — the dashboard.

  The order is an order of URGENCY, not of category, and it is the
  mockup's: what is broken, then who uses what, then how full each volume
  is, then the destinations that are not on this server.

  A location in error is stated with its CONSEQUENCE rather than as a red
  badge: « en erreur » tells an administrator that something is wrong,
  « les sauvegardes distantes ne partent plus » tells them what it is
  costing, and only the second sentence gets acted on this week.
#}
{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Stockage — {{ site_name }}{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
    {% include 'partials/page_header.html.twig' with {
        title: 'Stockage',
        subtitle: "Où ce site écrit ses fichiers, et ce qu'il y a dessus.",
    } only %}

    {% include 'config/storage/_nav.html.twig' with {current_path: current_path} only %}

    <div class="card mb-4">
        <div class="card-header py-2"><span class="fw-semibold small">État</span></div>

        {% for location in failing %}
            <div class="card-body border-bottom">
                <div class="d-flex flex-wrap justify-content-between align-items-center gap-2">
                    <span>{{ location.label }}</span>
                    <span class="badge text-bg-danger">En erreur</span>
                </div>
                <p class="small text-body-secondary mt-1 mb-1">
                    {{ location.lastCheckError }}
                    {# The consequence, derived from who actually stands on it rather
                       than guessed: « Sauvegardes distantes » is the consumer's own
                       French name for itself. #}
                    {% set served = [] %}
                    {% for row in usages %}
                        {% if location.label in row.locations %}
                            {% set served = served|merge([row.usage]) %}
                        {% endif %}
                    {% endfor %}
                    {% if served is not empty %}
                        <span class="d-block">{{ served|join(', ') }} : plus rien ne peut être écrit ici.</span>
                    {% endif %}
                </p>
                <a href="/config/stockage/emplacements" class="small">Corriger</a>
            </div>
        {% else %}
            <div class="card-body border-bottom">
                <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-0">
                    <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    Tous les emplacements déclarés répondent.
                </p>
            </div>
        {% endfor %}

        {# **What no archive covers.** A separate line from « en erreur »
           because it is a different kind of trouble: an unreachable
           location is a fault to correct today, an unprotected one is a
           state of affairs to decide about. Both belong in « État », and
           an administrator who reads only this card has to come away
           knowing both.

           Since IT-04 it is a real filter: the locations with no copy
           at all, and the ones whose copy is paused. A paused relation
           counts as unprotected on purpose — what this block answers is
           « what would I lose tonight », and a copy that is not running
           protects exactly nothing. #}
        {% if unprotected is not empty %}
            <div class="card-body border-bottom">
                <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-1">
                    <i class="bi bi-shield-exclamation text-warning" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <span class="fw-medium">Ces emplacements n'ont pas de copie de secours qui tourne.</span>
                </p>
                <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-0">
                    {{ unprotected|length ~ (unprotected|length == 1 ? ' emplacement est concerné' : ' emplacements sont concernés') }} :
                    {{ unprotected|map(l => l.label)|join(', ') }}.
                    Aucune archive ne reprend leur contenu&nbsp;: une sauvegarde restaurée
                    rendra les fiches, pas les fichiers.
                    Une copie se déclare sur la fiche de l'emplacement.
                </p>
            </div>
        {% endif %}

        <div class="card-body">
            <div class="text-uppercase small fw-semibold text-body-secondary mb-2">Usages</div>
            {% for row in usages %}
                <div class="d-flex justify-content-between border-bottom py-1 small">
                    <span>{{ row.usage }}</span>
                    <span class="text-body-secondary">
                        {{ row.locations is not empty ? row.locations|join(', ') : 'aucun emplacement' }}
                    </span>
                </div>
            {% else %}
                <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-0">
                    Rien n'utilise encore d'emplacement de stockage sur ce site.
                </p>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>

    <p class="small text-body-secondary px-1">
        L'espace se mesure <strong>par volume</strong>, pas par emplacement : deux dossiers sur le même
        disque partagent la même place libre, et les afficher séparément laisserait croire qu'on en a
        deux fois plus.
    </p>

    {% for volume in volumes %}
        <div class="card mb-4">
            <div class="card-header py-2"><span class="fw-semibold small">{{ volume.label }}</span></div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <div class="small text-body-secondary mb-1">
                    {% for directory in volume.directories %}
                        <code>{{ directory.path }}</code>{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}
                    {% endfor %}
                    {# The label comes from the object, not from a ternary
                       here: basis() has THREE answers, and the two-way
                       ternary this replaces printed « mesure système » for
                       the third — contradicting `volume.basisSentence`, a
                       few lines below on this same card. #}
                    · {{ volume.basisLabel }}
                </div>

                {% if volume.usedPercent is not null %}
                    {# Decorative: the percentage is spelled out in words
                       immediately below, and a bar repeating it only makes it
                       read twice — the same choice the Maintenance page made
                       for the panel this one replaces. #}
                    <div aria-hidden="true" class="progress mb-2" style="height: 6px;">
                        <div class="progress-bar" style="width: {{ volume.usedPercent }}%"></div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-0">
                        <strong>{{ volume.basisUsedLabel }}</strong> sur {{ volume.basisTotalLabel }} —
                        {{ volume.usedPercent }} %.
                    </p>
                {% elseif volume.occupiedLabel %}
                    <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-0">
                        <strong>{{ volume.occupiedLabel }}</strong> occupés. Aucune taille totale connue pour
                        ce volume.
                    </p>
                {% else %}
                    <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-0">Occupation inconnue pour ce volume.</p>
                {% endif %}

                {% if volume.directories|length > 1 %}
                    <div class="mt-2 small text-body-secondary">
                        {% for directory in volume.directories %}
                            <div class="d-flex justify-content-between border-bottom py-1">
                                <span>{{ directory.label }}</span>
                                <span class="text-body-secondary">
                                    {% if not directory.exists %}
                                        dossier absent
                                    {% elseif directory.sizeBytes is null %}
                                        taille inconnue
                                    {% else %}
                                        {{ directory.sizeLabel }}
                                    {% endif %}
                                </span>
                            </div>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </div>
                {% endif %}

                <p class="small text-body-secondary mt-2 mb-0">{{ volume.basisSentence }}</p>

                {% if volume.hasDirectoryOutsideStorage %}
                    <div class="alert alert-warning small mt-2 mb-0">
                        <strong>Ce volume porte un dossier hors de <code>storage/</code>.</strong>
                        Il n'est donc pas effacé par une réinitialisation complète du site — et il n'est
                        pas repris non plus dans les archives de sauvegarde.
                    </div>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
        </div>
    {% endfor %}

    {% if remote_locations is not empty %}
        <div class="card mb-4">
            <div class="card-header py-2"><span class="fw-semibold small">Emplacements distants</span></div>
            {% for location in remote_locations %}
                <div class="card-body border-bottom">
                    <div class="d-flex flex-wrap justify-content-between align-items-center gap-2">
                        <span>{{ location.label }}</span>
                        <span class="small text-body-secondary">occupation inconnue</span>
                    </div>
                    {#
                      Nothing rather than a bar that would be wrong. S3 cannot say
                      what a bucket occupies without walking it entirely, and a
                      progress bar drawn on a guess is read as a measurement.
                      IT-07 gives the types that CAN answer (WebDAV, Drive) a real
                      figure here.
                    #}
                    <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-0">
                        Ce type de stockage ne sait pas dire ce qu'il contient sans le parcourir entièrement.
                        Mieux vaut ne rien afficher qu'une barre fausse.
                    </p>
                </div>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    <p class="small text-body-secondary px-1">
        L'état de chaque emplacement est vérifié par écriture d'un fichier témoin, au plus toutes les
        {{ health_ttl_minutes }} minutes. Un dossier réseau peut disparaître, passer en lecture seule ou
        figer sans répondre : le test écrit réellement, avec un délai maximal.
    </p>
{% endblock %}
